From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:03:21 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] acp_thread: message times on the receipt transport too

0087 records when each message was sent: the agent's
_meta.claudeCode.timestamp when it sends one, else the time Zeo received the
message -- but only while a turn is running, because a replayed chunk received
now says nothing about when it was sent. "A turn is running" was written as
self.running_turn.is_some(), and running_turn exists only on the completion
transport, the ACP v1 path. The Zed Agent (since upstream #65420) and every
ACP v2 session submit through receipts and report their own activity
instead; running_turn stays None there. So those threads recorded no time at
all: neither for the user's message, which the Zed Agent inserts with
upsert_local_user_message rather than through send_inner, nor for a reply
without a timestamp of its own. Found by the upstream-native review of
2026-11-15 (docs/UPSTREAM-NATIVE-REVIEW.md in the hub, defect 5).

  - is_receiving_live: a turn this client runs, or Running / RequiresAction
    reported by the agent (foreground_activity, which upstream derives for
    every transport). The receive-time fallback and turn_duration's "still
    being written" check both use it; v1 replays still record nothing.
  - upsert_local_user_message stamps the message when it is sent, through the
    new record_message_time, which note_message_time now calls as well.
  - keyed_message_location, which creates every keyed entry on the receipt
    transport, pushed onto entries directly rather than through push_entry,
    so those entries got no message_times slot: nothing could be recorded on
    them, and every slot pushed afterwards landed one entry early. It now
    resizes message_times to entries once, after creating the entry.
  - update_keyed_message, the whole-message upsert the receipt transport uses
    for user, agent and thought messages, recorded no time at all: only
    append_message_chunk called note_message_time. It now does too, with the
    message's own metadata, so the same rule applies on both paths.

Test: message_times_are_recorded_on_a_receipt_session (Red on the series
before this patch).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

diff --git a/crates/acp_thread/src/acp_thread.rs b/crates/acp_thread/src/acp_thread.rs
index 986688c..c086153 100644
--- a/crates/acp_thread/src/acp_thread.rs
+++ b/crates/acp_thread/src/acp_thread.rs
@@ -5088,7 +5088,7 @@ impl AcpThread {
             .find(|(_, entry)| matches!(entry, AgentThreadEntry::UserMessage(_)))
             .map(|(ix, _)| ix);
         // The last turn is still being written while one runs: no duration until it ends.
-        if next_turn.is_none() && self.running_turn.is_some() {
+        if next_turn.is_none() && self.is_receiving_live() {
             return None;
         }
         let end = next_turn.unwrap_or(self.entries.len());
@@ -5100,10 +5100,22 @@ impl AcpThread {
         (replied - sent).to_std().ok()
     }
 
+    /// Whether a message arriving now belongs to work happening now rather than to history: a
+    /// turn this client runs (`running_turn`, the completion transport), or work the agent
+    /// reports (`foreground_activity`, the receipt transport the Zed Agent and every ACP v2
+    /// session use, where `running_turn` stays `None` -- 0131).
+    fn is_receiving_live(&self) -> bool {
+        self.running_turn.is_some()
+            || matches!(
+                self.foreground_activity(),
+                ForegroundActivity::Running | ForegroundActivity::RequiresAction
+            )
+    }
+
     /// Records a message chunk's time on the entry it went into: the agent's
-    /// `_meta.claudeCode.timestamp`, else the receive time while a turn runs. A replayed chunk
-    /// with no time of its own records nothing -- received now says nothing about when it was
-    /// sent.
+    /// `_meta.claudeCode.timestamp`, else the receive time while the thread receives live work.
+    /// A replayed chunk with no time of its own records nothing -- received now says nothing
+    /// about when it was sent.
     fn note_message_time(
         &mut self,
         entry_index: usize,
@@ -5117,10 +5129,15 @@ impl AcpThread {
         }
         let Some(time) = meta
             .and_then(agent_message_time)
-            .or_else(|| self.running_turn.is_some().then(chrono::Utc::now))
+            .or_else(|| self.is_receiving_live().then(chrono::Utc::now))
         else {
             return;
         };
+        self.record_message_time(entry_index, time);
+    }
+
+    /// Widens the time span recorded for the message at `entry_index` to include `time`.
+    fn record_message_time(&mut self, entry_index: usize, time: chrono::DateTime<chrono::Utc>) {
         if let Some(slot) = self.message_times.get_mut(entry_index) {
             *slot = Some(match *slot {
                 Some(known) => MessageTime {
@@ -6368,7 +6385,16 @@ impl AcpThread {
     ) -> Result<()> {
         let previous_entry_count = self.entries.len();
         let location = self.keyed_message_location(kind, id, cx)?;
-        self.replace_message_content(location, kind, content, meta, previous_entry_count, cx)
+        // A whole-message upsert is how the receipt transport delivers most messages, so it
+        // records a time as append_message_chunk does (0131); read before `meta` is applied.
+        let time_meta = match &meta {
+            MetadataUpdate::V1(MaybeUndefined::Value(meta))
+            | MetadataUpdate::V2(MaybeUndefined::Value(meta)) => Some(meta.clone()),
+            _ => None,
+        };
+        self.replace_message_content(location, kind, content, meta, previous_entry_count, cx)?;
+        self.note_message_time(location.entry_index(), time_meta.as_ref());
+        Ok(())
     }
 
     fn replace_message_content(
@@ -6534,7 +6560,7 @@ impl AcpThread {
 
         self.flush_streaming_text(cx);
         let entry_index = self.entries.len();
-        match kind {
+        let location = match kind {
             MessageKind::User => {
                 self.entries
                     .push(AgentThreadEntry::UserMessage(UserMessage {
@@ -6597,7 +6623,12 @@ impl AcpThread {
                     })
                 }
             }
-        }
+        };
+        // These entries bypass push_entry, so give them their message-time slot here: without
+        // it no time is recorded on a keyed message, and every slot after it shifts onto the
+        // wrong entry (0131).
+        self.message_times.resize(self.entries.len(), None);
+        location
     }
 
     fn emit_message_update(
@@ -8591,6 +8622,8 @@ impl AcpThread {
         message
             .content
             .replace_prompt(content, &language_registry, path_style, cx);
+        // A local message is sent now; the Zed Agent inserts its user messages this way (0131).
+        self.record_message_time(location.entry_index(), chrono::Utc::now());
         self.emit_message_update(location, previous_entry_count, cx);
         cx.notify();
         Ok(())
diff --git a/crates/acp_thread/src/acp_thread_message_times_tests.rs b/crates/acp_thread/src/acp_thread_message_times_tests.rs
index 2e2f466..fe58429 100644
--- a/crates/acp_thread/src/acp_thread_message_times_tests.rs
+++ b/crates/acp_thread/src/acp_thread_message_times_tests.rs
@@ -188,3 +188,50 @@ async fn message_times_follow_a_rewind(cx: &mut TestAppContext) {
         );
     });
 }
+
+/// The Zed Agent (since #65420) and every ACP v2 session submit through receipts and report their
+/// own activity: `running_turn` stays `None` there, so times keyed on it never recorded and those
+/// threads showed none (upstream-native review, defect 5). A local message is stamped when it is
+/// sent, and an agent message with no time of its own while the agent reports work.
+#[gpui::test]
+async fn message_times_are_recorded_on_a_receipt_session(cx: &mut TestAppContext) {
+    init_test(cx);
+    let (thread, _connection) = new_receipt_test_thread(cx).await;
+    thread.update(cx, |thread, cx| {
+        thread
+            .upsert_local_user_message(ClientUserMessageId::new(), vec!["Fix the build".into()], cx)
+            .expect("a local message");
+        thread
+            .update_session_state(
+                acp_v2::StateUpdate::Running(acp_v2::RunningStateUpdate::new()),
+                cx,
+            )
+            .expect("a receipt session reports its activity");
+        thread
+            .upsert_assistant_message(
+                acp_v2::AgentMessage::new("reply").content(vec!["On it.".into()]),
+                cx,
+            )
+            .expect("the reply");
+    });
+
+    thread.read_with(cx, |thread, _| {
+        let entries = thread.entries();
+        let user = entries
+            .iter()
+            .position(|entry| matches!(entry, AgentThreadEntry::UserMessage(_)))
+            .expect("the user message");
+        let reply = entries
+            .iter()
+            .position(|entry| matches!(entry, AgentThreadEntry::AssistantMessage(_)))
+            .expect("the reply");
+        assert!(
+            thread.message_time(user).is_some(),
+            "the local message is stamped when it is sent"
+        );
+        assert!(
+            thread.message_time(reply).is_some(),
+            "the reply is stamped when received while the agent reports work"
+        );
+    });
+}
